  "rationale": "No technique can be skipped, because each step creates a condition that only it (or an equal-length alternative) can provide. 1) phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. 2) pivot_internal gives reach_internal. 3) auth_appserver gives foothold_appserver. 4) kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin, the only way to get it. 5) auth_dc gives foothold_dc. 6) escalate_dc gives admin_dc. 7) dump_dbadmin_dc gives stolen_dbadmin, which needs admin_dc or admin_adfs. 8) auth_db gives foothold_db. 9) escalate_db gives admin_db. 10) exfiltrate_db gives exfiltrated. Every exfiltration technique needs an admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of those needs a foothold from an auth step that requires stolen_dbadmin. The only path to stolen_dbadmin is foothold, escalate and dump on the DC or ADFS, which in turn needs stolen_admin from kerberoasting. Kerberoasting needs an app or API server foothold, which needs reach_internal and stolen_user, which need an initial foothold."
